THE GATE-LANE-SHIFT TRIAL — owner ruling 2026-08-20, verbatim "ok, try that"
(to the recommendation: shift the middle crowd's lane ~6wu off the stake/spawn line)

Implemented as CrowdFlockSystem.GATE_LANE_SHIFT, applied only to a lane that would otherwise sit
ON the loss stake. The flank lanes never move. The crossing target is unchanged (the wheel plaza),
so the shifted crowd angles in.

VERIFIED THE LANE ACTUALLY MOVED, both seeds:
  flock-1@(-20,-30)->copper-pavilion   flock-2@(-6,-30)->ferris-wheel   flock-3@(20,-30)->silver-pavilion

── THE A/B, ON ONE INSTRUMENT ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Identical free-standing fort (radius-8 palisade ring + 4 inner beacons, placed at t=0), identical
1 gold/second repair stream at repair-under-60%, identical upgrade priority, both bench seeds,
wave ceiling 14. The ONLY variable is the lane.

  lane x =  0 (as ratified)   seed 01 crossings [5,3,7]   seed 02 crossings [4,4,3]   BOTH SECURE
  lane x = -6 (ruled shift)   seed 01 crossings [5,0,7]   seed 02 crossings [4,0,5]   neither

The flanks are unchanged in both columns (5/7 and 4/5), so the instrument is sound: the only crowd
that moved is the only crowd that changed, and it went from three and four crossings to NONE.

A second arm, with the rider's own west wall pushed out to x=-12 to give the shifted crowd its
fright radius back, and six guns moved clear of its lane:
  lane x = -6, wall -12       seed 01 crossings [2,0,5]   seed 02 crossings [4,0,6]   neither
Still zero. Widening the fort did not buy the crossing back; it only cost construction.

── WHY, MEASURED ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
1. THE OFFSET DECAYS EXACTLY WHERE IT IS NEEDED. The crowd still walks to the wheel at (0,8), so
   its lane is a diagonal and its clearance from the runners' line is 6.0wu at the gate, 4.4 at
   z=-20, 2.8 at z=-10 and 1.9 at the north spawn point itself — inside the fright radius of 7 for
   the whole corridor. Scatter positions from the shifted run read the decay off directly:
     t37  F2 at (-5,-26) by night_runner@(-12,-24) d=6.9
     t63  F2 at (-4,-19) by night_runner@(-3,-13)  d=6.9
     t110 F2 at (-5,-23) by night_runner@(-2,-17)  d=6.9
     t207 F2 at (-4,-18) by night_runner@(-7,-11)  d=6.9
     t373 F2 at (-6,-27) by night_runner@(-6,-21)  d=6.9
2. THE STAKE IS ALSO THE SHIELD. Everything on this claim walks AT (0,-30) from all three spawn
   edges, so everything the hero kills, it kills closing on that tile — and a crowd waiting there
   sits inside the tightest part of that cover. Six units aside took the crowd out of the shield
   without taking it out of the traffic. Two of the shifted run's scatters are saboteurs at
   (-10,-22) and (-11,-22): the besiegers followed the crowd west, because the wall did.

── VERDICT ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
The trial was run and the answer is NO. GATE_LANE_SHIFT ships at 0 — the lever stays implemented,
documented and one number from live, and the pre-ruling geometry is unchanged, so no spec pin, no
floor and no census number moves. The ruling covered ONE lane shift, not an iterative geometry
search, so the measurement stops here. What it recommends instead is on the desk as F-E3CF-3.

NEUTRALITY OF THE LANDED CHANGE, PROVEN BY REPRODUCTION rather than asserted: the prover that
secured bench seed 01 before this work was re-run against the edited engine at GATE_LANE_SHIFT=0
and returned fnv1a32:9f2740ab, secured=true, wave 12 — the same hash, to the digit.


════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
THE SECOND RULING — "move the spawn" (owner, 2026-08-20, verbatim)
════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

WHERE THE SPAWN LIVES. Engine-derived, not contract data:
  src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:557   const radius = Balance.waves.spawnRingRadius;      (26)
  src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:562   edge 'north' -> (center.x + lateral, center.z + radius)
  src/systems/WaveSystem.ts:531   center = territoryRingSpawnCenter(wave) -> heroPosition (0,-30)
  => north entry = (0 +- jitter, -4)   — matches the measured (0,-4.1) exactly.

THE SEAM USED, and the one deliberately NOT used:
  NOT `tileParams.noSpawnZones` — src/meta/ContractFamilies.ts:705 declares it
      "Birth-loader output only (tile-persistence sim entries) — never authored in contract JSON",
      and e2e/tp02-green-waypoint.spec.ts:200 guards that law. Authoring it would break it.
  USED `ContractEnemyVariant.spawnGates` (ContractFamilies.ts:373/381), consumed by
      WaveSystem.applyVariantSpawnGate:576 — authored per VARIANT and per EDGE, already carried by
      16 entries across four epochs (two of them in this very epoch file). Fairground-only,
      night_runner-only, no shared spawn code touched.

THE DECAY TABLE that chose the offset. A runner entering at (X,-4) walks to the stake at (0,-30),
so its clearance from the middle lane at height z is |X| x (z+30)/26:

        z:      -4     -10    -14    -18    -22
   X = -6:     6.0     4.6    3.7    2.8    1.8
   X = -8:     8.0     6.2    4.9    3.7    2.5
   X = -12:   12.0     9.2    7.4    5.5    3.7
   X = -13:   13.0    10.0    8.0    6.0    4.0     (but only 7.0 from the flank lane at x=-20)

-12 clears the fright radius down to z~-13.6 — the lane's swept length above where the fort's own
guns reach — while still leaving 8wu to the flank crowd's lane at x=-20, so the fix does not move
the problem onto a different crowd. -13 buys 0.6wu more and spends the flank's whole margin.

MEASURED, same free-fort instrument as above (radius-8 ring + 4 beacons, 1 g/s repairs, both seeds):

   gate (0,-4)   baseline    seed 01 [5,3,7]    seed 02 [4,4,3]    frights 29 / 33   both secure
   gate (-12,-4)             seed 01 [4,10,7]   seed 02 [3,8,3]    frights 22 / 29   both secure
   gate (+12,-4)             seed 01 [8,9,6]    seed 02 [5,6,1]    frights 20 / 35   both secure
   gate (-8,-4)              seed 01 [8,7,7]    seed 02 [5,7,3]    frights 20 / 28   both secure
   gate (+8,-4)              seed 01 [8,4,7]    seed 02 [6,4,3]    frights 24 / 31   both secure

The middle crowd goes from 3 and 4 crossings to 10 and 8 at -12 — the best of the five — and total
frights FALL on both seeds, which is the mechanism showing itself: the runner stream stopped
sweeping the lane. -12 is landed. +12 is nearly as good on seed 01 but costs the east flank crowd
(1 crossing on seed 02), so the west shoulder is the better shoulder.

⚠️ AND THE PUBLIC-VERB PROVER REGRESSED ON IT — F-E3CF-6 CAME DUE, EXACTLY AS FLAGGED.
   prover-v2 on the old gate: seed 01 SECURED w12 fnv1a32:9f2740ab · seed 02 w14 fnv1a32:afdd8c2a
   prover-v2 on the new gate: seed 01 w5  fnv1a32:f0ec6b1e · seed 02 w4  fnv1a32:31392949
   Income collapsed 800 -> 200 and 705 -> 175 gold panned; the wheel survived; the hero did not.
   The middle crowd DID cross for the rider on seed 02 ([0,1,0]) — the escort half works.
   Four re-tunes (beacons 4/6 x maxWorks 14/22 x minTrip 45/70) did not recover it; best was
   seed 01 w14 [4,0,2] at 625 panned, still unsecured.
   CAUSE, as predicted: the securing fort was ACCIDENT-SHAPED — two unplaceable beacon spots
   capped construction at ~14 works and left the rest of the purse for upkeep. Moving the runners
   off the lane changed which walls take the pressure, and an accidental shape does not travel.

VERDICT: the MAP is better and the RIDER is not yet funded for it. The admission hold STANDS —
both seeds must secure through the public door and today neither does. The map change is kept
because the controlled instrument says it strictly improves the ratified objective, and nothing is
claimed that is not proven: the exemption row, the census refusal, the door baseline and the floors
are all untouched.
